  "slug": "dark-energy-543b",
  "summary": "New reconstructions, model comparisons and independent SN Ia pipelines probe the DESI-driven w0–wa departure from ΛCDM and its systematics.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is whether DESI BAO or full-shape data, combined with CMB, supernova and lensing probes, require dark energy beyond a cosmological constant. Within VCDM, three one-parameter vacuum histories are compared. F42 is favored by AIC when supernovae are included, while Bayesian evidence is assessed separately. A DESI DR1 full-shape analysis finds that the scalar-field Fading Dark Sector model outperforms CPL w0–wa. Two non-parametric reconstructions of the effective dark-energy density and gravitational response report a phantom-divide crossing near z≈0.5–0.7. One of them also asks whether dark energy clusters. A proposed set of 0i Einstein-equation tests uses observables alone to separate gravity, dark energy and dark matter. On supernova systematics, LEMAITRE and a ZTF/SNLS/HSC calibration effort provide independent SN Ia data to test the w–w_a tension. A forecast asks whether Simons Observatory and CMB-S4 can distinguish w0waCDM from ΛCDM shadow models. Separate preprints address 21 cm signatures of boosted dark matter and the effect of astrophysical priors on pulsar-timing-array evidence for new physics.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
